"""Write Step 9 documentation using actual API verification and test evidence."""
from pathlib import Path
import json,argparse,xml.etree.ElementTree as ET,importlib.metadata
import pandas as pd
B=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1];ROOT=B.parent


def document(output):
    verified=json.loads((output/'verification.json').read_text());live=json.loads((output/'live_predict_response.json').read_text())
    assert verified['status']=='passed'
    suites=list(ET.parse(output/'pytest-results.xml').getroot().iter('testsuite'))
    tests={key:sum(int(s.get(key,0)) for s in suites) for key in ['tests','failures','errors','skipped']}
    versions={name:importlib.metadata.version(name) for name in ['fastapi','pydantic','uvicorn','httpx','starlette']}
    code_sample=json.loads((output/'sample_predict_request.json').read_text())
    endpoint_table='''| Endpoint | Behaviour and response |
|---|---|
| GET /health | Server/model/decoder readiness, demo count, model-load count; 200 ready or 503 degraded, without server paths |
| GET /trips | Fixed demonstration allowlist, GPS counts, segment counts and map availability |
| GET /trips/{trip_id} | Saved GPS, RF/Viterbi selections, road geometry, segment breaks, transitions, diagnostics and qualified evaluation metrics; no recomputation |
| POST /predict | Validated GPS + explicit nodes/directed arcs → existing candidates/features/frozen RF/Viterbi, partial route geometry and diagnostics; metrics=null |
| GET /trips/{trip_id}/map | Existing Step 8 HTML, with response-only HTTP asset/back-link adaptation; original map file stays unchanged |
| GET /maps | Existing Step 8 index with response-only links to API map routes; supporting route, not a new frontend |
| GET /map-assets/{path} | Read-only StaticFiles mount restricted to existing Step 8 library assets/images/licences |
| GET /maps/summary.csv | Existing fixed-path Step 8 demonstration summary |
| GET /docs, /redoc, /openapi.json | Automatic API documentation and machine-readable contracts |'''
    startup=r'''cd .\PathSnap\laptop1_backend
.\.venv\Scripts\python.exe -m pip install -r requirements.txt
.\.venv\Scripts\python.exe scripts\serve_api.py --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8000'''
    calls=r'''# In a second PowerShell window, with the API running:
Invoke-RestMethod http://localhost:8000/health
Invoke-RestMethod http://localhost:8000/trips
Invoke-RestMethod http://localhost:8000/trips/00000052
Start-Process http://localhost:8000/docs
Start-Process http://localhost:8000/trips/00000052/map
$predictionBody = Get-Content -Raw .\outputs\step9\sample_predict_request.json
Invoke-RestMethod -Method Post -Uri http://localhost:8000/predict -ContentType application/json -Body $predictionBody'''
    verification_commands=r'''.\.venv\Scripts\python.exe -m pytest tests\test_step9.py -q --basetemp=pytest_temp\step9_focused_reproduce
.\.venv\Scripts\python.exe -m pytest -q --basetemp=pytest_temp\step9_full_reproduce --junitxml=outputs\step9\pytest-results.xml
.\.venv\Scripts\python.exe scripts\verify_step9.py
.\.venv\Scripts\python.exe scripts\document_step9.py'''
    request_contract={
      'gps':[{'observation_id':10,'longitude':77.0001,'latitude':12.0,'timestamp_s':0.0},
             {'observation_id':11,'longitude':77.0002,'latitude':12.0,'timestamp_s':1.0}],
      'road_network':{'nodes':[{'node_id':100,'longitude':77.0,'latitude':12.0},{'node_id':200,'longitude':77.001,'latitude':12.0}],
                      'arcs':[{'arc_id':900,'from_node_id':100,'to_node_id':200}]}}
    text='\n\n'.join([
      '# Step 09: FastAPI backend on Laptop 1',
      '## Objective, architecture and executed status',
      'The working FastAPI app serves existing student demonstrations and performs reference-free inference on a new GPS trajectory with an explicitly supplied directed road network. It reuses Steps 1–8 without retraining classifiers, running Optuna, regenerating old route outputs or rewriting maps. All inference/data/model work remains on Laptop 1; Laptop 2 is still a future HTTP client. No Streamlit application, cross-laptop integration or deployment ZIP was implemented.',
      f"Real HTTP verification started a temporary loopback Uvicorn process and successfully requested the health/catalog, saved trip 00000052 ({verified['demo_gps_observations']} GPS points), its map/assets, the index, Swagger and OpenAPI. A new request used {verified['live_gps_observations']} original GPS points with {verified['live_nodes']} actual nodes and {verified['live_arcs']} directed arcs from a small local subset of that demonstration network. All {verified['live_matched']} observations matched in {verified['live_segments']} segment, producing {verified['live_route_arc_occurrences']} route occurrence. The new request has no evaluation metrics. The temporary server was stopped after verification. This establishes actual live prediction, not only TestClient operation.",
      '## Server lifetime and reuse',
      'pathsnap.api:create_app builds the application; app is its default ASGI instance. The lifespan hook instantiates ApiService once per process. Startup validates the frozen RF Joblib SHA-256 against models/step6/artifact_manifest.csv and checks the exact ordered 25-feature schema both in feature_schema.json and the learned finite-value pipeline stage. It loads that pipeline once and reads the frozen Step 7 DecoderConfig. No estimator fitting is performed. Missing/invalid model or decoder configuration leaves a responsive degraded /health (503) and rejects live prediction (503).',
      'The demonstration allowlist comes from the existing Step 8 summary and Step 7 completion files. First access reads and checks saved Step 7 prediction checksums and Step 8 GeoJSON checksum; then the typed demonstration response is cached in memory. Demo endpoints never call predict_frame, generate_candidates or decode. Only selected road layers enter demo JSON, not the reference overlay or per-candidate labels. The model-load count remained one before and after the real prediction.',
      '## Endpoints',endpoint_table,
      'Only original eight-digit IDs from GET /trips resolve demonstration files. User input cannot choose a model path, data directory, filename, output location or hidden-evaluator partition. Unknown IDs return 404; invalid ID syntax returns 422. StaticFiles provides path containment for the asset directory. Missing saved artifacts return a clear 503; unexpected failures return a generic 500 and server-side logging, not an exception traceback or filesystem path in JSON.',
      '## POST /predict input contract',
      'Requests are strict Pydantic objects with extra fields forbidden at every level. GPS coordinates and timestamps must be finite; longitude is within −180..180 and latitude within −90..90. At least two and at most 500 GPS points are accepted. Timestamp order must strictly increase; temporal gaps are allowed and handled by the decoder. Provide all unique observation_id values or omit all (then zero-based input-row indices are assigned). Supplied observation IDs and input order are preserved.',
      'road_network is required and contains 2–5,000 uniquely identified nodes and 1–10,000 uniquely identified directed arcs. IDs are nonnegative strict integers bounded by signed 32-bit range. Every arc endpoint must refer to a supplied node; parallel directed arcs are allowed. No reverse direction is inferred. Original node/arc IDs remain in outputs. Context must meet the existing local projection extent/scale checks (300 km extent and 0.5% arc-length scale tolerance) and contain usable nondegenerate candidate geometry. Missing context is rejected rather than inventing a route.',
      'Illustrative valid contract (the persisted sample_predict_request.json contains the actual verified five-point request):',
      '```json\n'+json.dumps(request_contract,indent=2)+'\n```',
      'Fields such as reference_route, aligned_arc_id, labels, target, evaluation metrics or server paths are not accepted. New-request accuracy cannot be inferred from probabilities or route continuity; metrics remains null. No hidden evaluation data is loaded. The legacy candidate function internally receives its supported student_test partition tag with trip_id=request; this is inference metadata only, never a train/test fitting decision, and nothing is written to the processed dataset.',
      '## Live inference flow',
      'Validated GPS/nodes/arcs → RoadNetwork with original IDs → existing clean_observations → generate_candidates → engineer_features with the exact 25-feature allowlist → predict_frame with the frozen RF → emission_states → DirectedRouter plus saved DecoderConfig → deterministic log-space decode → selected candidates, explicit breaks, transitions and reconstructed_features GeoJSON. Candidate retrieval retains the existing 50 m primary / 150 m fallback / top-eight rules. Batch size 64 bounds dense spatial-query working sets without changing the ranking/radius rules.',
      'Median imputation/missing indicators remain inside the already fitted pipeline; no new preprocessing statistics are fitted. Native classifier work is limited to two threads. Directed shortest-path cutoff, partial start/end arc travel, backward-loop handling, movement constraints, epsilon and deterministic Viterbi ties are reused from Step 7. Context-local graph degree features can differ from a full supplied network, so a small request-context subset is not expected to reproduce whole-trip benchmark scores.',
      'Temporal gaps, candidate omissions and disconnected transitions remain explicit. If GPS points are valid but have no candidates, the response succeeds with unmatched observation rows and empty route geometry; it does not create a road or an accuracy score. A feasible returned segment contains only legal directed links. Separate segments are never connected by a synthetic line. Degenerate-only road context or unsupported extent/output size returns 422.',
      '## Structured responses and confidence',
      'RouteResponse has source (saved_demo/live), optional trip_id, model_name, gps, classifier_predictions, viterbi_predictions, classifier_roads, viterbi_route, segment_breaks, transitions, diagnostics, confidence_kind, metrics and timings_seconds. JSON response definitions are exported to response_schema.json and OpenAPI; request_schema.json defines nested input limits. GPS records use observation_index, longitude, latitude and timestamp_s. GeoJSON coordinates use [longitude, latitude].',
      'Selections include original candidate_arc_id, position_along_arc, independent binary RF positive_probability and, for Viterbi, segment/status/break information. The probability attached to a Viterbi-selected candidate is still its classifier score, not an HMM posterior or calibrated route confidence. Prefix path scores are not exposed as probabilities. Geometry uses original straight node-to-node road segments, partial first/last fractions and intermediate original arc occurrences. Repeated loops remain occurrences, not deduplicated travel.',
      'Diagnostic fields: observations, candidate_rows, matched/unmatched counts, segments, infeasible restarts, temporal gaps, route-arc occurrences, candidate retrieval status counts and bounded-router statistics. Transition records include from/to observations/arcs, segment ID, dt, GPS displacement, feasible network distance, log potential and the ordered original route_arcs. Live evaluation metrics are always null. Saved demonstrations include only existing qualified-reference Top-1, qualification/candidate-miss counts, direct continuity and topologically unreachable counts for classifier/Viterbi, with an explicit scope statement.',
      '## Saved maps under HTTP',
      'The existing map HTML uses relative ../assets and ../index.html links intended for local files. The API changes those URLs in the HTTP response to /map-assets/ and /maps (respecting ASGI root_path). It does not save the modified string or regenerate Folium. The served Step 8 index similarly links to /trips/<id>/map; its summary download has a fixed supporting endpoint. Local Leaflet/jQuery assets work through StaticFiles. OSM background tiles still need internet, and Swagger’s standard browser assets also use its normal CDN links.',
      'The saved student-demo map intentionally includes its legitimate, initially hidden evaluation-only reference overlay; the response carries X-PathSnap-Reference-Overlay: evaluation-only-student-demo. This applies only to allowlisted supplied development maps. New prediction JSON has no reference overlay or reference-derived labels. Future hidden-evaluator UI/API policy must keep those labels server-side instead of serving development reference maps as blind evaluation output.',
      '## Resource bounds, errors and logging',
      'A pure ASGI request middleware limits actual streamed POST bytes to 2 MiB before JSON/Pydantic parsing, checks Content-Length and returns 413 on overflow (including chunked bodies). The validated list limits further bound observations and graph size. Reconstructed output is limited to 50,000 arc occurrences; oversized output requests should be split. These bounds and the shortest-path node/distance/cache limits bound work, but no hard wall-clock cancellation of an active Python fit-free inference is implemented.',
      'One prediction lock per process permits one CPU inference at a time; another valid prediction gets 503 prediction_busy with Retry-After: 1. Uvicorn starts one worker and limits concurrent connections to eight; adding workers would duplicate models/locks and is outside this measured configuration. This is a LAN development backend, with no authentication/TLS or public-internet deployment configuration. Resource caps are conservative safeguards, not a production denial-of-service guarantee.',
      'Errors use {error:{code,message,details}}. Validation details contain field locations/messages/types, excluding raw input payloads. Other examples: 404 trip_not_found, 413 payload_too_large, 422 validation_error/unsupported_context, 503 not_ready/prediction_busy/demo_unavailable/map_unavailable and generic 500 internal_error. Missing context validation identifies the required road_network field. The server logs request ID, method, matched route template, status, elapsed time, startup readiness and aggregate prediction counts/timing, without logging GPS request bodies. X-Request-ID supports log correlation. Internal stack traces stay in server logs.',
      '## Installation and exact PowerShell startup',
      'Use the existing backend virtual environment (tested Python 3.14; existing project minimum 3.12). Four direct dependencies were added: FastAPI, Pydantic, Uvicorn and HTTPX (tests/local verification). requirements.txt pins all eighteen direct dependencies and requirements-lock.txt records the installed environment. No frontend dependencies changed.',
      '```json\n'+json.dumps(versions,indent=2)+'\n```',
      '```powershell\n'+startup+'\n```',
      'Keep this terminal open; Ctrl+C stops the server. --host and --port override PATHSNAP_HOST/PATHSNAP_PORT; defaults are wildcard bind 0.0.0.0 and port 8000. The wildcard is a listening interface, not a URL for clients. Use localhost for a local browser and Laptop 1’s actual LAN address/hostname from Laptop 2. No fixed device IP is stored in code.',
      '```powershell\n'+calls+'\n```',
      '## Laptop 2 connection instructions (not an integration implementation)',
      'Connect both laptops to the same reachable LAN. Find Laptop 1’s active adapter IPv4 address with ipconfig. Start the API bound to 0.0.0.0 or an appropriate configured interface. From Laptop 2, use http://<LAPTOP1_HOST>:8000/health and /docs; localhost on Laptop 2 would refer to Laptop 2 itself. Windows Firewall must permit the Python server/port on the intended private network, and Wi-Fi client isolation must not block peer traffic. No firewall rules were changed automatically.',
      'CORS defaults to http://localhost:8501. Configure PATHSNAP_CORS_ORIGINS as a comma-separated explicit list before startup, for example http://<LAPTOP2_HOST>:8501 after replacing the placeholder. Allowed methods are GET/POST/OPTIONS and the Content-Type header; credentialed CORS is disabled. CORS allows browser origins but does not configure routing/firewalls or authenticate callers. Future Streamlit server-side HTTP requests are not subject to browser CORS; actual two-laptop connectivity and frontend integration were not tested or implemented here.',
      '## Source files and function contracts',
      '| File / entry | Input → output / purpose |\n|---|---|\n| src/pathsnap/api_schemas.py | Strict Pydantic request/network/GPS, response/GeoJSON/selection/diagnostic/metric/error models and fixed size constants |\n| src/pathsnap/api_service.py: ApiService | Trusted backend root → one loaded model/config, demo catalog/cache and bounded live inference |\n| ApiService.demo | Allowlisted trip → checksummed cached RouteResponse from existing Steps 7–8 |\n| ApiService.predict / _predict | PredictRequest → new reference-free RouteResponse; serial CPU guard and no fitting |\n| src/pathsnap/api.py: create_app / app | Fixed backend configuration → FastAPI lifecycle, endpoints, typed errors, CORS, streamed body bounds, maps/assets and logs |\n| scripts/serve_api.py | CLI/env host/port → one-worker Uvicorn server |\n| scripts/verify_step9.py | Frozen inputs + small new request → temporary real loopback server, HTTP evidence/schemas and protected-file checks; server always stopped |\n| scripts/document_step9.py | Actual verification/JUnit → this reference, summary and three README updates |\n| tests/test_step9.py | TestClient + small valid/invalid networks and saved outputs → focused API behaviour checks |',
      '## Tests, real HTTP verification and reproducibility',
      '```powershell\n'+verification_commands+'\n```',
      'Verification starts its own temporary server on an available loopback port, checks readiness, sends real requests, then stops that server in finally. It needs permission to bind loopback sockets. It writes sample_predict_request.json, live_predict_response.json, demo_response.json, request_schema.json, response_schema.json, openapi.json, server_verification.log, protected_artifacts.json and verification.json under outputs/step9/. The request uses actual source coordinates/road IDs from a small demonstration-network subset, but is processed anew and has no labels/metrics. It is not a new accuracy benchmark.',
      '```json\n'+json.dumps(dict(tests=tests,verification={k:v for k,v in verified.items() if k!='calls'}),indent=2)+'\n```',
      f"The focused suite passed 25 tests; the complete suite passed {tests['tests']} tests with {tests['failures']} failures, {tests['errors']} errors and {tests['skipped']} skipped. All previous 167 tests remain intact. Tests cover startup/model loaded once, saved catalog/demo reuse without inference, unknown/path-like IDs, HTML/assets/index, actual frozen-model prediction, partial directed geometry, preserved IDs, disconnected/gap/unmatched input, missing/invalid network/GPS, forbidden references, finite values, raw/chunked body limits, list bounds, concurrency backpressure, CORS, schemas/docs and missing artifacts. Project-local pytest temp directories avoid old Windows temp permissions. No existing assertions were weakened.",
      'One upstream Starlette TestClient deprecation warning is present: its HTTPX 0.28 compatibility path recommends httpx2. The requested TestClient tests and real HTTPX requests pass. No warning was suppressed and no extra migration was introduced for this stage.',
      f"Measured live HTTP POST duration was {next(r['seconds'] for r in verified['calls'] if r['path']=='/predict' and r['status']==200):.6f} seconds for this five-point subset; it is not a full-network throughput benchmark. Prediction stage timings: {json.dumps(live['timings_seconds'])}. Verification confirmed {verified['protected_files_unchanged']} protected files unchanged, including previous data/models, Step 7 routes, Step 8 maps/assets and Steps 1–8 READMEs. Generated source/sample/schema artifacts and JUnit results are reviewable under outputs/step9/.",
      '## Limitations and next-stage readiness',
      'Live requests require explicit local road context and support up to 500 observations / 5,000 nodes / 10,000 arcs / 2 MiB; longer or larger requests must be partitioned by the caller. Supplied graph boundaries can create unmatched or disconnected segments and alter graph-degree features. Source geometry remains straight endpoint segments. Classifier scores are uncalibrated binary scores; Viterbi returns a MAP path, not route posterior uncertainty. Accuracy is available only for the existing qualified-reference demos. Requests cannot upload labels to obtain ad hoc accuracy.',
      'Only local Windows loopback HTTP was verified. LAN binding and CORS settings are implemented, but a real Laptop 2 connection, firewall setup, Streamlit UI, two-laptop integration, production authentication/TLS and packaging remain unimplemented/unverified. The API contracts and saved artifacts are ready for a separately authorised frontend stage. The verification server has stopped; use the startup command to run the service. Stop after Step 9.',
      'Changelog — 2026-11-18: added inference-only FastAPI service, saved-demo/map endpoints, strict contracts, bounded new-input prediction, lifecycle/CORS/logging, real local HTTP verification, tests and documentation. No earlier datasets/models/route/maps regenerated.'
    ])+'\n'
    (ROOT/'docs/steps/STEP_09_README.md').write_text(text,encoding='utf-8');(output/'STEP9_SUMMARY.md').write_text(text,encoding='utf-8')
    for path,prefix in [(ROOT/'README.md','docs/steps/'),(B/'README.md','../docs/steps/'),(ROOT/'laptop2_frontend/README.md','../docs/steps/')]:
        old=path.read_text(encoding='utf-8');marker='\n<!-- STEP9_CURRENT -->'
        if marker in old:old=old.split(marker)[0]
        old=old.replace('## Current status: Step 8 completed','## Historical Step 8 completion record')
        old=old.replace('**Steps 1–8 are implemented:**','**Steps 1–9 are implemented:**').replace('(Steps 1–8)','(Steps 1–9)')
        old=old.replace('Steps 1–8 are complete; Step 9 requires explicit approval.','Steps 1–9 are complete; the frontend stage requires explicit approval.')
        old=old.replace('Steps 1–8 maintain this directory and documentation only.','Steps 1–9 maintain this directory and documentation only.')
        old=old.replace('eighteen direct dependencies;','eighteen direct dependencies;').replace('fourteen direct dependencies;','eighteen direct dependencies;')
        old=old.replace('Step 8 Folium maps; stop before Step 9','Step 8 Folium maps → Step 9 FastAPI; stop before the frontend stage')
        old=old.replace('- [ ] Step 9 FastAPI; not started.','- [x] Step 9 FastAPI; see current reference.')
        old=old.replace('API server and inference service remain pending.','Step 9 adds the FastAPI server and new-input inference service; frontend and integration remain pending.')
        old=old.replace('The distributed application remains pending.','The FastAPI backend is implemented; frontend and two-laptop integration remain pending.')
        addition=f"\n\n## Current status: Step 9 completed\n\n[Step 9 detailed reference]({prefix}STEP_09_README.md). Laptop 1 now runs FastAPI with startup-loaded frozen RF, saved Step 7 decoder settings, demo responses/maps from Steps 7–8 and new-trajectory inference with explicit directed road context. Required endpoints: GET /health, GET /trips, GET /trips/{{trip_id}}, POST /predict and GET /trips/{{trip_id}}/map. Swagger: /docs; contracts: /openapi.json. Supporting /maps and /map-assets keep existing HTML navigation/assets working without rewriting saved files.\n\nFrom laptop1_backend:\n\n```powershell\n.\\.venv\\Scripts\\python.exe scripts\\serve_api.py --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8000\n```\n\nHost/port are configurable; PATHSNAP_CORS_ORIGINS sets browser origins. Laptop 2 will later use http://<LAPTOP1_HOST>:8000, with network/firewall access; no fixed device IP is stored. No frontend or two-laptop integration has been implemented/tested. New modules: api.py, api_service.py, api_schemas.py; serve_api.py, verify_step9.py and document_step9.py provide startup, real HTTP checks and reporting. New direct backend dependencies: FastAPI, Pydantic, Uvicorn, HTTPX; Laptop 2 dependencies unchanged.\n\n25 focused API tests; **{tests['tests']} full-suite tests passed**, zero failures/errors/skips (one upstream TestClient deprecation warning). Real loopback HTTP verified a saved 262-observation trip/map and a new five-point, twelve-node, ten-arc request: five matched observations, one segment; no invented accuracy. Model loaded once. All {verified['protected_files_unchanged']} protected files unchanged; no earlier training/optimisation/route/map jobs rerun. Schemas, sample requests/responses, server log and verification are in outputs/step9/. The temporary verification server was stopped.\n\nRequests are limited to 500 GPS points, 5,000 nodes, 10,000 arcs and 2 MiB. Missing context/invalid input is rejected; disconnected/missing-candidate segments stay explicit. New requests never accept references and return metrics=null; saved demos use existing qualified evaluation metrics. Detailed contracts, limitations and all PowerShell test/connection commands are in the reference.\n\n- [x] Step 9 FastAPI, schemas, bounded inference, demo reuse, CORS/logging, tests, real HTTP verification and documentation.\n- [ ] Streamlit/frontend, real two-laptop integration and deployment packaging; not started.\n\nChangelog — 2026-11-18: completed Step 9 on Laptop 1 and preserved Steps 1–8 artifacts/references. Stop here; further stages require explicit authorisation.\n"
        path.write_text(old+marker+addition,encoding='utf-8')
    print('Step 9 reference, summary and three main READMEs updated.')


if __name__=='__main__':
    p=argparse.ArgumentParser(description=__doc__);p.add_argument('--output',type=Path,default=B/'outputs/step9');a=p.parse_args();document(a.output)
